var e={id:`switzerland`,name:`Switzerland`,localName:`Schweiz / Suisse / Svizzera`,flag:`🇨🇭`,currency:`CHF`,language:`German, French, Italian`,greeting:{text:`Grüezi`,meaning:`Hello (Swiss German, polite)`},bestMonths:[1,2,6,7,8,9,12],tips:[`Trains, boats and buses run like clockwork: a Swiss Travel Pass covers most of them plus museums and gives discounts on mountain railways, while the Half Fare Card halves almost every fare.`,`Install the SBB Mobile app for timetables, platform numbers and tickets; buy before you board, as there are no ticket sales on most trains.`,`Tap water is excellent and free, including from the many public fountains, so carry a refillable bottle.`,`Most shops close on Sundays and by 18:00–19:00 on weekdays; station and airport shops stay open late and on Sundays.`,`Switzerland is expensive: mountain railways can cost CHF 100–250 return, so save with supermarket picnics from Migros or Coop.`,`Mountain weather changes fast: check the summit webcams before buying excursion tickets and bring layers, sunscreen and sunglasses even in summer.`],cities:[{id:`zurich`,name:`Zürich`,lat:47.37444,lng:8.54111,timezone:`Europe/Zurich`,tagline:`Old-town lanes, lake swims and the thundering Rhine Falls`,description:`Switzerland's biggest city wraps a medieval old town around the Limmat river and the north shore of Lake Zurich, with first-rate museums, chocolate shops and a lively bar scene in the former industrial west. Fast trains make it an easy base for the Rhine Falls, Stein am Rhein and the lakeside rose town of Rapperswil.`,idealDays:[2,4],places:[{id:`altstadt-niederdorf`,name:`Old Town & Niederdorf`,localName:`Altstadt`,category:`culture`,tags:[`old-town`,`walking`,`heritage`,`free`,`cafes`,`iconic`],area:`Altstadt`,lat:47.37315,lng:8.54364,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`A web of cobbled lanes, guild houses and hidden squares on both banks of the Limmat; the pedestrian Niederdorf on the east side is lined with cafés, bars and small shops.`,tip:`Wander the quieter lanes around Spiegelgasse and Rindermarkt, where Lenin once lived and Dada was born.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Altstadt (Zurich)`},{id:`grossmunster`,name:`Grossmünster`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`church`,`iconic`,`viewpoint`,`reformation`,`architecture`],area:`Altstadt`,lat:47.37014,lng:8.54399,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:5,description:`The twin-towered Romanesque church that symbolises Zürich, where Zwingli launched the Swiss Reformation; climb the Karlsturm for views over the rooftops and lake.`,tip:`Church entry is free; the tower climb has a small fee and closes around 17:00 (earlier in winter).`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Grossmünster`},{id:`fraumunster`,name:`Fraumünster`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`stained-glass`,`chagall`,`art`,`rainy-day`],area:`Altstadt`,lat:47.36972,lng:8.54111,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:4,description:`A slender-spired church famous for five luminous stained-glass windows by Marc Chagall in the choir, plus a rose window by Augusto Giacometti.`,tip:`Entry includes an audio guide; photography of the windows is not allowed inside.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Fraumünster`},{id:`st-peter`,name:`St. Peter Church`,localName:`St. Peter`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`church`,`clock`,`old-town`,`free`],area:`Altstadt`,lat:47.3711,lng:8.54069,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Zürich's oldest parish church, whose tower carries one of the largest church clock faces in Europe, nearly nine metres across.`,tip:`Pair it with Lindenhof just uphill and the Fraumünster a few minutes away.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`St. Peter, Zurich`},{id:`lindenhof`,name:`Lindenhof`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`park`,`roman`,`free`,`photo-spot`],area:`Altstadt`,lat:47.37305,lng:8.54065,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A tree-shaded hilltop square on the site of a Roman fort, with a classic view across the Limmat to the university and the Grossmünster towers.`,tip:`Locals play giant chess here; it is lovely at dusk when the old town lights come on.`,indoor:!1},{id:`bahnhofstrasse`,name:`Bahnhofstrasse`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`shopping`,`luxury`,`watches`,`chocolate`,`free`],area:`City`,lat:47.37139,lng:8.53865,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`One of the world's most expensive shopping streets, running from the main station to the lake past watchmakers, banks, department stores and chocolatiers.`,tip:`Shops close by 18:00 or 20:00 and almost everything is shut on Sundays.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bahnhofstrasse`},{id:`confiserie-sprungli`,name:`Confiserie Sprüngli, Paradeplatz`,category:`food`,tags:[`chocolate`,`sweets`,`cafe`,`iconic`,`rainy-day`],area:`Paradeplatz`,lat:47.36948,lng:8.53914,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`The flagship of Zürich's grand confectioner since 1859, selling truffles and the airy little Luxemburgerli macarons, with an old-world café upstairs.`,tip:`Luxemburgerli are best eaten within a couple of days, so buy a small box to enjoy on the go.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Confiserie Sprüngli`},{id:`swiss-national-museum`,name:`Swiss National Museum`,localName:`Landesmuseum Zürich`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`castle-style`,`swiss-culture`,`rainy-day`],area:`Hauptbahnhof`,lat:47.37917,lng:8.53972,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:13,rating:4,description:`A fairy-tale castle of a building beside the main station telling the story of Switzerland from prehistory to today, with period rooms, armour and changing exhibitions.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; open late on Thursdays. Covered by the Swiss Museum Pass and Swiss Travel Pass.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Swiss National Museum`},{id:`kunsthaus-zurich`,name:`Kunsthaus Zürich`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`modern-art`,`giacometti`,`monet`,`rainy-day`],area:`Heimplatz`,lat:47.3703,lng:8.5481,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`Switzerland's largest art museum, strong on Giacometti, Munch, Monet and Swiss painters, with a bold new extension by David Chipperfield.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; Wednesdays are free for the permanent collection.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Kunsthaus Zürich`},{id:`lake-zurich-cruise`,name:`Lake Zurich Boat Cruise`,localName:`Zürichsee-Schifffahrt`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`boat`,`lake`,`scenic`,`summer`],area:`Bürkliplatz`,lat:47.3665,lng:8.54077,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`Public lake boats leave from Bürkliplatz for short round trips past lakeside villas and vineyards, with the Glarus Alps on the horizon on clear days.`,tip:`The short round trip is covered by a ZVV zone ticket or the Swiss Travel Pass; sunset sailings run in summer.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lake Zurich`},{id:`uetliberg`,name:`Uetliberg`,category:`nature`,tags:[`mountain`,`viewpoint`,`hiking`,`sunset`,`train`],area:`Uetliberg`,lat:47.34944,lng:8.49139,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:4,description:`Zürich's own mountain, 25 minutes by S10 train from the main station, with a lookout tower over the city, lake and, on clear days, the Alps.`,tip:`Walk the gentle Planet Trail along the ridge to Felsenegg (about 2 hours) and ride the cable car down to Adliswil.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Uetliberg`},{id:`polybahn-eth-terrace`,name:`Polybahn & ETH Terrace`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`funicular`,`viewpoint`,`university`,`sunset`],area:`Central`,lat:47.37639,lng:8.54389,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:2,rating:3,description:`A little red funicular from 1889 climbs from Central to the ETH university, whose broad terrace gives one of the best views over the old town.`,tip:`The ride is short enough to walk back down through the old town afterwards.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Polybahn`},{id:`rhine-falls`,name:`Rhine Falls`,localName:`Rheinfall`,category:`nature`,tags:[`waterfall`,`day-trip`,`boat`,`iconic`,`family`],area:`Neuhausen am Rheinfall`,lat:47.67722,lng:8.61583,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:5,description:`Europe's most powerful waterfall, where the Rhine plunges 23 metres over a 150-metre-wide rock shelf; boats ferry you right up to the rock in the middle of the falls.`,tip:`Take the train to Schloss Laufen am Rheinfall station (about 50 minutes) for the viewing platforms; flow peaks in June and July.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Rhine Falls`},{id:`stein-am-rhein`,name:`Stein am Rhein`,category:`culture`,tags:[`old-town`,`day-trip`,`painted-houses`,`medieval`,`photo-spot`],area:`Stein am Rhein`,lat:47.66,lng:8.8592,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A small medieval town on the Rhine whose main square is lined with richly painted, half-timbered façades, overlooked by Hohenklingen castle.`,tip:`Combine it with the Rhine Falls in one day, or take the summer boat along the Rhine from Schaffhausen.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Stein am Rhein`},{id:`rapperswil`,name:`Rapperswil Castle & Rose Town`,category:`culture`,tags:[`castle`,`day-trip`,`roses`,`lake`,`old-town`],area:`Rapperswil`,lat:47.22667,lng:8.81833,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A lakeside town at the far end of Lake Zurich with a hilltop castle, rose gardens with hundreds of varieties and a long wooden pilgrim bridge across the water.`,tip:`In summer go out by boat from Zürich (about 2 hours) and return by fast S-Bahn (about 35 minutes).`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Rapperswil Castle`},{id:`fifa-museum`,name:`FIFA Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`football`,`sport`,`interactive`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Enge`,lat:47.36351,lng:8.53175,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:32,rating:3,description:`A slick, interactive museum of world football with the World Cup trophy, kits from every member nation and a pinball-style game hall.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; book online for a small discount.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`FIFA Museum`},{id:`lindt-home-of-chocolate`,name:`Lindt Home of Chocolate`,category:`family`,tags:[`chocolate`,`museum`,`tasting`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Kilchberg`,lat:47.3184,lng:8.5511,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`Lindt's showpiece chocolate museum next to its factory, with a nine-metre chocolate fountain, a history of Swiss chocolate and generous tastings.`,tip:`Book a timed ticket online, especially at weekends; take the S8 train or the lake boat to Kilchberg.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Lindt Home of Chocolate`},{id:`zoo-zurich`,name:`Zürich Zoo & Masoala Rainforest`,localName:`Zoo Zürich`,category:`family`,tags:[`zoo`,`animals`,`rainforest`,`kids`],area:`Zürichberg`,lat:47.38442,lng:8.57468,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:37,rating:4,description:`A large, well-designed zoo on the wooded Zürichberg, highlighted by the Kaeng Krachan elephant park and the walk-through Masoala rainforest hall.`,tip:`Tram 6 runs from the main station to the gate; the Masoala hall makes it a decent rainy-day choice.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Zürich Zoologischer Garten`},{id:`rietberg-museum`,name:`Rietberg Museum`,localName:`Museum Rietberg`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`asian-art`,`african-art`,`villa`,`park`,`rainy-day`],area:`Enge`,lat:47.3589,lng:8.5304,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`Art from Asia, Africa, the Americas and Oceania, shown in a 19th-century villa and a modern glass pavilion set in the leafy Rieterpark.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; the park around it is free and pleasant for a stroll.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Rietberg Museum`},{id:`chinese-garden-zurichhorn`,name:`Chinese Garden & Zürichhorn`,localName:`Chinagarten`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`garden`,`lake`,`park`,`sunset`,`summer`],area:`Seefeld`,lat:47.355,lng:8.55194,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:3,description:`A walled Chinese garden, a gift from Zürich's twin city Kunming, beside the lakeside lawns of Zürichhorn park, where locals picnic and swim.`,tip:`The garden opens only from spring to autumn and closes at 19:00; the park and lakeshore stay open after dark.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Chinese Garden, Zurich`},{id:`flussbad-oberer-letten`,name:`Flussbad Oberer Letten`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`swimming`,`river`,`summer`,`bar`,`free`,`local`],area:`Kreis 5`,lat:47.38457,lng:8.53631,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A free river bath on the Limmat where locals float downstream on hot days, then linger at the bars along the canal into the evening.`,tip:`Open roughly May to September; the current is strong, so only confident swimmers should jump in.`,indoor:!1},{id:`im-viadukt`,name:`Im Viadukt`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`design`,`market-hall`,`boutiques`,`local`],area:`Zürich West`,lat:47.38774,lng:8.52639,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Shops, studios and cafés tucked into the stone arches of a 19th-century railway viaduct, anchored by a covered food market hall.`,tip:`Most shops are closed on Sundays; the market hall is busiest at Saturday lunchtime.`,indoor:!0},{id:`frau-gerolds-garten`,name:`Frau Gerolds Garten`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`beer-garden`,`containers`,`summer`,`drinks`,`local`],area:`Zürich West`,lat:47.38517,lng:8.51906,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`An urban garden of shipping containers, flower beds and long tables beside the railway tracks, with drinks and grills in summer and a cosy fondue hut in winter.`,tip:`Next to the Freitag tower of stacked containers, which has a free rooftop viewing deck.`,indoor:!1},{id:`langstrasse`,name:`Langstrasse Nightlife`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`clubs`,`multicultural`,`late-night`],area:`Kreis 4`,lat:47.37627,lng:8.52667,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`Zürich's former red-light street is now its busiest nightlife strip, packed with bars, small clubs, kebab shops and late-night eateries.`,tip:`It gets lively from about 22:00 on Fridays and Saturdays; keep an eye on your belongings in the crowds.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Langstrasse`},{id:`zurich-opera-house`,name:`Zürich Opera House`,localName:`Opernhaus Zürich`,category:`culture`,tags:[`opera`,`ballet`,`performance`,`architecture`],area:`Bellevue`,lat:47.365,lng:8.54694,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:90,rating:4,description:`A neo-baroque opera house on the lakefront staging opera and the Ballett Zürich, with high standards and an intimate auditorium.`,tip:`Cheaper restricted-view and standing tickets are released shortly before performances.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Zurich Opera House`},{id:`tonhalle-zurich`,name:`Tonhalle Zürich`,category:`culture`,tags:[`concert`,`classical`,`music`,`architecture`],area:`Enge`,lat:47.36599,lng:8.53766,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:70,rating:3,description:`A gilded 1895 concert hall with famously fine acoustics, home of the Tonhalle Orchestra and touring soloists.`,tip:`The season runs September to June; lunchtime and late-evening short concerts are cheaper.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Tonhalle, Zurich`}],foods:[{name:`Zürcher Geschnetzeltes`,description:`Thin strips of veal in a creamy white-wine and mushroom sauce, the city's signature dish, almost always served with rösti.`},{name:`Rösti`,description:`A golden pan-fried cake of grated potato, crisp outside and tender inside, eaten as a side or topped with cheese and egg.`},{name:`Kalbsbratwurst`,description:`A pale veal sausage grilled until browned, served in the hand with a crusty bürli roll and mustard from street stands.`},{name:`Luxemburgerli`,description:`Bite-sized, feather-light macarons in rotating flavours, a Sprüngli speciality since the 1950s.`},{name:`Cheese Fondue`,localName:`Käsefondue`,description:`A shared pot of melted cheese with white wine and kirsch, scooped up with cubes of bread on long forks.`}]},{id:`lucerne`,name:`Lucerne`,localName:`Luzern`,lat:47.05,lng:8.30944,timezone:`Europe/Zurich`,tagline:`Wooden bridges, paddle steamers and peaks on the doorstep`,description:`A storybook lakeside town of painted squares, medieval walls and covered wooden bridges, set where the Reuss leaves Lake Lucerne. Paddle steamers, cogwheel trains and cable cars fan out to Pilatus, Rigi, Titlis and the meadow where Switzerland was founded.`,idealDays:[2,4],places:[{id:`chapel-bridge`,name:`Chapel Bridge`,localName:`Kapellbrücke`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`bridge`,`iconic`,`medieval`,`free`,`photo-spot`],area:`Old Town`,lat:47.05167,lng:8.3075,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Europe's oldest covered wooden bridge, built in the 14th century, angles across the Reuss beside its stone Water Tower, with painted panels under the roof.`,tip:`Cross early morning before the tour groups, then come back after dark when the bridge and tower are lit.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Kapellbrücke`},{id:`old-town-squares`,name:`Old Town Squares`,localName:`Altstadt Luzern`,category:`culture`,tags:[`old-town`,`painted-facades`,`walking`,`free`],area:`Old Town`,lat:47.05201,lng:8.30482,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A compact car-free old town of guild houses with frescoed façades around the Weinmarkt, Hirschenplatz and Kornmarkt squares.`,tip:`A twice-weekly market (Tuesday and Saturday mornings) sets up along the river below the old town hall.`,indoor:!1},{id:`spreuer-bridge`,name:`Spreuer Bridge`,localName:`Spreuerbrücke`,category:`culture`,tags:[`bridge`,`medieval`,`paintings`,`free`],area:`Old Town`,lat:47.05191,lng:8.30174,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The city's second covered bridge, quieter than the Chapel Bridge, with a haunting cycle of 17th-century Dance of Death paintings in its gables.`,tip:`Look upstream to the Needle Dam, a hand-operated weir that still regulates the lake level.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Spreuer Bridge`},{id:`musegg-wall`,name:`Musegg Wall`,localName:`Museggmauer`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`city-walls`,`towers`,`viewpoint`,`free`,`medieval`],area:`Old Town`,lat:47.05381,lng:8.30207,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A long stretch of the medieval town wall with nine towers above the old town; four can be climbed, including the Zyt tower with the city's oldest clock.`,tip:`Open roughly April to early November; the Männliturm gives the widest view over roofs, lake and Pilatus.`,indoor:!1},{id:`jesuit-church`,name:`Jesuit Church`,localName:`Jesuitenkirche`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`baroque`,`riverside`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Old Town`,lat:47.05053,lng:8.30519,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Switzerland's first large baroque church, a riverside landmark with onion-domed towers and a dazzling white and pink stucco interior.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Jesuit Church, Lucerne`},{id:`hofkirche`,name:`Church of St. Leodegar`,localName:`Hofkirche`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`renaissance`,`organ`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Hof`,lat:47.0557,lng:8.31405,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The city's main church, rebuilt in late-Renaissance style after a 1633 fire, with twin Gothic spires, carved altars and a celebrated organ.`,tip:`Look into the arcaded cemetery around the church, lined with old family tombs.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Church of St. Leodegar (Lucerne)`},{id:`lion-monument`,name:`Lion Monument`,localName:`Löwendenkmal`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`monument`,`sculpture`,`history`,`free`,`iconic`],area:`Wesemlin`,lat:47.05845,lng:8.31089,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A dying lion carved into a sandstone cliff above a pond, honouring the Swiss Guards killed defending the Tuileries in Paris in 1792.`,tip:`It is next door to the Glacier Garden and the Bourbaki Panorama, so do all three together.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lion Monument`},{id:`glacier-garden`,name:`Glacier Garden`,localName:`Gletschergarten`,category:`museum`,tags:[`geology`,`ice-age`,`mirror-maze`,`kids`],area:`Wesemlin`,lat:47.05892,lng:8.31041,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:28,rating:3,description:`Giant potholes ground into the rock by Ice Age meltwater, plus a museum, a walk through the rock and an Alhambra-style mirror maze that children love.`,indoor:!0},{id:`bourbaki-panorama`,name:`Bourbaki Panorama`,category:`museum`,tags:[`panorama`,`painting`,`history`,`rainy-day`],area:`Wesemlin`,lat:47.05697,lng:8.31122,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:19,rating:3,description:`A 112-metre circular painting from 1881 showing a defeated French army crossing into Switzerland in winter 1871, an early humanitarian mission of the Red Cross.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Bourbaki Panorama`},{id:`swiss-museum-of-transport`,name:`Swiss Museum of Transport`,localName:`Verkehrshaus der Schweiz`,category:`family`,tags:[`trains`,`planes`,`planetarium`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Lido`,lat:47.05278,lng:8.33583,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`Switzerland's most visited museum: locomotives, cable cars, planes and ships, a planetarium, a chocolate ride and a giant walkable aerial map of the country.`,tip:`Arrive at opening to beat school groups; the lake boat stops right outside.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Swiss Museum of Transport`},{id:`rosengart-collection`,name:`Rosengart Collection`,localName:`Sammlung Rosengart`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`picasso`,`klee`,`modern-art`,`rainy-day`],area:`Pilatusstrasse`,lat:47.04968,lng:8.30732,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`A private collection with a remarkable depth of Picasso and Paul Klee, plus Monet, Cézanne and Chagall, in a former bank building near the station.`,indoor:!0},{id:`richard-wagner-museum`,name:`Richard Wagner Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`music`,`villa`,`lakeside`,`history`],area:`Tribschen`,lat:47.04239,lng:8.32904,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:19,rating:2,description:`The lakeside villa where Wagner lived from 1866 to 1872, now a small museum of his life and instruments with a peaceful park running down to the water.`,tip:`Open roughly mid-March to November and closed Mondays; a 30-minute lakeside walk from the station.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Tribschen`},{id:`lake-lucerne-cruise`,name:`Lake Lucerne Paddle Steamer Cruise`,localName:`Vierwaldstättersee`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`boat`,`paddle-steamer`,`lake`,`scenic`,`sunset`],area:`Bahnhofquai`,lat:47.05138,lng:8.31118,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:5,description:`Historic paddle steamers and modern ships zigzag across the fjord-like lake between mountains, villages and lakeside hotels, linking to the mountain railways.`,tip:`Boats are free with the Swiss Travel Pass and half price with the Half Fare Card; sit on the open upper deck.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lake Lucerne`},{id:`mount-pilatus`,name:`Mount Pilatus Golden Round Trip`,localName:`Pilatus`,category:`nature`,tags:[`mountain`,`cogwheel-railway`,`cable-car`,`viewpoint`,`iconic`,`day-trip`],area:`Pilatus`,lat:46.97926,lng:8.25564,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:150,rating:5,description:`Lucerne's dragon-legend mountain, reached by boat to Alpnachstad, the world's steepest cogwheel railway up, and gondolas down to Kriens on the classic Golden Round Trip.`,tip:`The cogwheel railway runs only from about May to November; in winter go up and down by gondola from Kriens.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Pilatus (mountain)`},{id:`rigi`,name:`Rigi`,category:`nature`,tags:[`mountain`,`cogwheel-railway`,`viewpoint`,`sunrise`,`hiking`,`day-trip`],area:`Rigi`,lat:47.05584,lng:8.48408,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:95,rating:5,description:`The Queen of the Mountains, an isolated summit with sweeping views over a dozen lakes, reached by Europe's first mountain railway from lakeside Vitznau.`,tip:`Go up by boat and cogwheel train from Vitznau, walk down a stretch through meadows, and return by cable car from Weggis.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Rigi`},{id:`titlis`,name:`Titlis`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`glacier`,`snow`,`cable-car`,`suspension-bridge`,`day-trip`],area:`Engelberg`,lat:46.7707,lng:8.4264,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:125,rating:4,description:`Snow year-round at 3,000 metres above Engelberg, with a rotating gondola, a glacier cave, the Titlis Cliff Walk suspension bridge and an ice-flyer chairlift over the glacier.`,tip:`Take the train to Engelberg (about 45 minutes); start early, as clouds often build after midday.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Titlis`},{id:`stanserhorn`,name:`Stanserhorn CabriO`,category:`nature`,tags:[`mountain`,`cable-car`,`open-top`,`viewpoint`,`marmots`],area:`Stans`,lat:46.92976,lng:8.34037,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:100,rating:4,description:`A vintage funicular and then the world's first open-top double-decker cable car lift you to a summit with a 360-degree panorama of lakes and Alps.`,tip:`Open roughly April to November; ride on the open roof deck for the full effect.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Stanserhorn`},{id:`hammetschwand-lift`,name:`Bürgenstock & Hammetschwand Lift`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`cliff-walk`,`elevator`,`viewpoint`,`boat`,`funicular`],area:`Bürgenstock`,lat:47.00111,lng:8.39639,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`A boat and funicular ride lead to a cliffside path on the Bürgenstock and Europe's highest outdoor elevator, which shoots 153 metres up the rock face.`,tip:`The cliff path and lift operate in the warmer months only; the boat-plus-funicular combo ticket is good value.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hammetschwand Elevator`},{id:`rutli`,name:`Rütli Meadow`,localName:`Rütli`,category:`culture`,tags:[`history`,`birthplace`,`boat`,`meadow`,`free`],area:`Uri`,lat:46.969,lng:8.593,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The lakeside meadow where, by tradition, the founders of the Swiss Confederation swore their oath in 1291, reached only by boat or on foot.`,tip:`Combine it with the Swiss Path lakeside trail or continue by boat to Flüelen.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Rütli`},{id:`gutsch`,name:`Gütsch Funicular & Viewpoint`,localName:`Gütsch`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`funicular`,`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`castle-hotel`],area:`Gütsch`,lat:47.0515,lng:8.295,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:2,rating:3,description:`A short funicular climbs to Château Gütsch, a turreted castle-hotel with a terrace looking over the old town, the lake and the mountains beyond.`,tip:`Go before sunset for a drink on the terrace, then walk back down through the woods.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Château Gütsch`},{id:`kkl-luzern`,name:`KKL Luzern`,localName:`Kultur- und Kongresszentrum Luzern`,category:`culture`,tags:[`concert`,`architecture`,`classical`,`lakeside`,`festival`],area:`Bahnhof`,lat:47.05,lng:8.312,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:70,rating:4,description:`Jean Nouvel's lakeside culture centre with a dramatic cantilevered roof and a world-class concert hall, home of the Lucerne Festival in summer.`,tip:`Even without tickets, the rooftop Kunstmuseum and the lakefront under the roof are worth a look.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Lucerne Culture and Congress Centre`},{id:`reuss-riverside-bars`,name:`Reuss Riverside Bars`,localName:`Rathausquai`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`riverside`,`terraces`,`beer`],area:`Old Town`,lat:47.05194,lng:8.30693,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`The arcaded riverbank below the old town hall fills with terraces after work, looking across the water to the floodlit Chapel Bridge.`,tip:`The house brewery under the old town hall arcades is a good first stop for a local beer.`,indoor:!1},{id:`grand-casino-luzern`,name:`Grand Casino Luzern`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`casino`,`bar`,`belle-epoque`,`lakeside`],area:`Haldenstrasse`,lat:47.05506,lng:8.31727,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:2,description:`A Belle Époque casino on the lakefront promenade with gaming tables, slot machines, a bar and lake-view terrace.`,tip:`Bring your passport; entry is from age 18 and smart-casual dress is expected.`,indoor:!0},{id:`schwanenplatz-shopping`,name:`Schwanenplatz Watch & Souvenir Shops`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`watches`,`swiss-army-knives`,`chocolate`,`souvenirs`],area:`Schwanenplatz`,lat:47.05335,lng:8.30863,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The square at the end of the Chapel Bridge and the lanes behind it are packed with big watch houses, pocket-knife shops and chocolatiers.`,tip:`Shops close by 18:30 on weekdays and early on Saturdays; most are shut on Sundays.`,indoor:!0},{id:`lido-lucerne`,name:`Lido Lucerne Beach`,localName:`Strandbad Lido`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`swimming`,`summer`,`lake`,`kids`],area:`Lido`,lat:47.0501,lng:8.33602,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`A big lakeside lido with sandy beach, lawns, pools and views straight across to Pilatus, next to the Museum of Transport.`,tip:`Open from about May to September; the lakefront path from the old town takes 30 minutes on foot.`,indoor:!1}],foods:[{name:`Luzerner Chügelipastete`,description:`Lucerne's own vol-au-vent: a large puff-pastry shell filled with veal, meatballs and mushrooms in a creamy sauce, often with raisins.`},{name:`Älplermagronen`,description:`Alpine herders' macaroni baked with potatoes, cream and cheese, topped with fried onions and served with apple sauce.`},{name:`Cheese Fondue`,localName:`Käsefondue`,description:`Melted cheese with white wine and garlic in a communal pot, eaten with bread on long forks, best on a cold evening.`},{name:`Luzerner Birnenweggen`,description:`A pastry roll filled with spiced dried pears, nuts and dried fruit, a central Swiss autumn and Christmas treat.`},{name:`Zuger Kirschtorte`,description:`A layered cake from neighbouring Zug: nut meringue and sponge soaked in cherry brandy, wrapped in butter cream.`}]},{id:`interlaken`,name:`Interlaken`,lat:46.6863,lng:7.8571,timezone:`Europe/Zurich`,tagline:`Two turquoise lakes below the Eiger, Mönch and Jungfrau`,description:`A resort town on a green plain between Lake Thun and Lake Brienz, and the gateway to the Jungfrau Region: cogwheel trains and cable cars climb to Jungfraujoch, Grindelwald First, Mürren and the Schilthorn, while waterfalls pour into the Lauterbrunnen valley below. It is also Switzerland's adventure-sports capital.`,idealDays:[3,5],places:[{id:`jungfraujoch`,name:`Jungfraujoch – Top of Europe`,localName:`Jungfraujoch`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`glacier`,`snow`,`cogwheel-railway`,`iconic`,`viewpoint`,`full-day`],area:`Jungfrau Region`,lat:46.54722,lng:7.98056,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:300,rating:5,description:`Europe's highest railway station at 3,454 metres, reached by train through the Eiger, with the Sphinx observation deck over the Aletsch Glacier, an ice palace and snow fun year-round.`,tip:`Check the summit webcams before buying, go on the earliest clear morning, and reserve a seat on the Eiger Express in high season.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Jungfraujoch`},{id:`grindelwald-first`,name:`Grindelwald First`,localName:`First`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`cliff-walk`,`zipline`,`gondola`,`hiking`,`lake`,`kids`],area:`Grindelwald`,lat:46.6608,lng:8.05469,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:110,rating:5,description:`A gondola from Grindelwald rises to First, with a steel cliff walk facing the Eiger, an easy hike to the mirror-like Bachalpsee, and the First Flyer zipline and mountain carts back down.`,tip:`Walk to Bachalpsee (about 1 hour each way) early for still-water reflections, then ride the First Flyer and Trottibikes down.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`First (Grindelwald)`},{id:`lauterbrunnen-staubbach-falls`,name:`Lauterbrunnen & Staubbach Falls`,localName:`Staubbachfall`,category:`nature`,tags:[`waterfall`,`valley`,`village`,`free`,`iconic`,`photo-spot`],area:`Lauterbrunnen`,lat:46.58965,lng:7.90551,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`A sheer-walled glacial valley with 72 waterfalls, where the Staubbach Falls drops nearly 300 metres beside the village church in a veil of spray.`,tip:`A free path climbs behind the falls in summer; the classic photo spot is on the road just south of the church.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Staubbach Falls`},{id:`trummelbach-falls`,name:`Trümmelbach Falls`,localName:`Trümmelbachfälle`,category:`nature`,tags:[`waterfall`,`inside-mountain`,`glacier-water`,`rainy-day`],area:`Lauterbrunnen`,lat:46.56907,lng:7.91498,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`Ten glacier-fed waterfalls thundering inside the mountain, reached by a tunnel lift and lit galleries; up to 20,000 litres a second drain the Eiger, Mönch and Jungfrau.`,tip:`Open roughly April to early November; bring a jacket, as it is cold and wet inside. Not suitable for small children.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Trümmelbach Falls`},{id:`murren`,name:`Mürren`,category:`culture`,tags:[`car-free`,`village`,`cliff`,`viewpoint`,`hiking`],area:`Lauterbrunnen`,lat:46.55944,lng:7.89222,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A car-free village of chalets perched on a cliff edge 800 metres above the Lauterbrunnen valley, staring straight at the Eiger, Mönch and Jungfrau.`,tip:`Arrive via the cable car to Grütschalp and the panoramic train, then walk down to Gimmelwald and take the cable car to Stechelberg.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Mürren`},{id:`schilthorn`,name:`Schilthorn – Piz Gloria`,localName:`Schilthorn`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`mountain`,`cable-car`,`revolving-restaurant`,`james-bond`,`viewpoint`],area:`Mürren`,lat:46.55722,lng:7.83528,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:140,rating:4,description:`A 2,970-metre summit with a revolving restaurant made famous by the Bond film On Her Majesty's Secret Service, plus the Thrill Walk along the cliff at Birg.`,tip:`The new direct cable cars from Stechelberg make it quicker; breakfast at Piz Gloria is a popular early-morning option.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Schilthorn`},{id:`harder-kulm`,name:`Harder Kulm`,category:`nature`,tags:[`funicular`,`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`two-lakes`],area:`Interlaken`,lat:46.69727,lng:7.85166,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:50,rating:4,description:`A ten-minute funicular from town to a platform hanging over both lakes, with the Eiger, Mönch and Jungfrau lined up across the valley.`,tip:`Runs from about April to November; on summer evenings stay for sunset and dinner at the turreted restaurant.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Harderkulm`},{id:`schynige-platte`,name:`Schynige Platte`,category:`nature`,tags:[`cogwheel-railway`,`alpine-garden`,`hiking`,`viewpoint`,`vintage`],area:`Wilderswil`,lat:46.65611,lng:7.90694,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:85,rating:4,description:`A vintage cogwheel train from 1893 climbs from Wilderswil to a ridge with an alpine botanical garden and a celebrated panorama trail high above Lake Brienz.`,tip:`Open only from late May to October; sit on the right going up for the best views.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Schynige Platte`},{id:`mannlichen`,name:`Männlichen Royal Walk & Panorama Trail`,localName:`Männlichen`,category:`nature`,tags:[`hiking`,`gondola`,`viewpoint`,`eiger`,`easy-walk`],area:`Grindelwald / Wengen`,lat:46.61806,lng:7.93806,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:85,rating:4,description:`A ridge between Grindelwald and Wengen with a short Royal Walk to a crown-shaped lookout and an easy, mostly downhill trail to Kleine Scheidegg facing the Eiger north face.`,tip:`Ride up from Grindelwald Terminal or Wengen, walk to Kleine Scheidegg (about 1.5 hours) and return by train.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Männlichen`},{id:`lake-brienz-cruise`,name:`Lake Brienz Cruise`,localName:`Brienzersee`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`boat`,`lake`,`turquoise`,`scenic`],area:`Interlaken Ost`,lat:46.6905,lng:7.869,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`Boats glide across the glacier-green Lake Brienz from Interlaken Ost to Iseltwald, Giessbach and the woodcarving village of Brienz.`,tip:`Free with the Swiss Travel Pass; services are frequent in summer and sparse from November to March.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lake Brienz`},{id:`lake-thun-cruise`,name:`Lake Thun Cruise`,localName:`Thunersee`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`boat`,`lake`,`castles`,`scenic`],area:`Interlaken West`,lat:46.6838,lng:7.8474,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`Larger Lake Thun is lined with castles, vineyards and villages such as Spiez and Oberhofen, with the pyramid-shaped Niesen rising from the shore.`,tip:`Hop off at Oberhofen or Spiez for a castle visit; summer evening cruises run on some dates.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lake Thun`},{id:`iseltwald`,name:`Iseltwald`,category:`nature`,tags:[`village`,`lake`,`pier`,`photo-spot`],area:`Lake Brienz`,lat:46.7106,lng:7.9636,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`A small fishing village on a peninsula in Lake Brienz, known for its lakeside chapel, a castle on the point and a wooden jetty made famous by a Korean TV drama.`,tip:`The jetty now has a turnstile with a small fee; arrive by boat for the prettiest approach.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Iseltwald`},{id:`giessbach-falls`,name:`Giessbach Falls`,localName:`Giessbachfälle`,category:`nature`,tags:[`waterfall`,`funicular`,`historic-hotel`,`hiking`],area:`Lake Brienz`,lat:46.73543,lng:8.02329,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:9,rating:4,description:`A waterfall tumbling in 14 tiers through the forest to Lake Brienz, reached by boat and Europe's oldest historic funicular, beside a grand 19th-century hotel.`,tip:`A footpath passes behind one of the cascades; the boat landing and funicular operate from April to October.`,indoor:!1},{id:`brienz-rothorn-railway`,name:`Brienz Rothorn Railway`,localName:`Brienz Rothorn Bahn`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`steam-train`,`cogwheel-railway`,`mountain`,`viewpoint`,`vintage`],area:`Brienz`,lat:46.75508,lng:8.03889,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:120,rating:4,description:`Steam locomotives push vintage carriages up a steep cogwheel line from Brienz to the 2,244-metre Rothorn, with views over the lake to the Bernese Alps.`,tip:`Runs June to October; the Swiss Travel Pass gives only a discount, so book steam departures ahead.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Brienz Rothorn Railway`},{id:`ballenberg`,name:`Ballenberg Open-Air Museum`,localName:`Freilichtmuseum Ballenberg`,category:`museum`,tags:[`open-air-museum`,`farmhouses`,`crafts`,`animals`,`kids`],area:`Brienz`,lat:46.74955,lng:8.08645,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:4,description:`More than 100 historic farmhouses rebuilt in a wooded park, with farm animals, gardens and craftspeople showing cheese-making, weaving and woodcarving.`,tip:`Open mid-April to October; the park is large, so pick the east or west entrance according to what you want to see.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Ballenberg`},{id:`st-beatus-caves`,name:`St. Beatus Caves`,localName:`St. Beatus-Höhlen`,category:`nature`,tags:[`caves`,`stalactites`,`legend`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Sundlauenen`,lat:46.68467,lng:7.78231,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:28,rating:3,description:`A kilometre of lit caverns, waterfalls and dripstone above Lake Thun, linked to the legend of a monk who drove out a dragon.`,tip:`Open roughly March to November; the bus from Interlaken West takes about 10 minutes. It stays around 10°C inside.`,indoor:!0},{id:`aare-gorge`,name:`Aare Gorge`,localName:`Aareschlucht`,category:`nature`,tags:[`gorge`,`boardwalk`,`river`,`hiking`],area:`Meiringen`,lat:46.71778,lng:8.21361,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:3,description:`A walkway clings to the walls of a narrow limestone gorge carved by the Aare, sometimes just a metre wide and 200 metres deep.`,tip:`Combine with Meiringen, home of the meringue and the Reichenbach Falls of Sherlock Holmes fame.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Aare Gorge`},{id:`oeschinen-lake`,name:`Oeschinen Lake`,localName:`Oeschinensee`,category:`nature`,tags:[`lake`,`hiking`,`gondola`,`unesco`,`photo-spot`],area:`Kandersteg`,lat:46.49833,lng:7.72694,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`An intensely blue mountain lake ringed by cliffs and waterfalls above Kandersteg, with a classic panorama trail along the slopes above it.`,tip:`Take the train to Kandersteg via Spiez, then the gondola; the panorama trail needs a head for heights.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Oeschinen Lake`},{id:`thun-castle`,name:`Thun Castle`,localName:`Schloss Thun`,category:`museum`,tags:[`castle`,`medieval`,`history`,`viewpoint`,`rainy-day`],area:`Thun`,lat:46.75992,lng:7.62972,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:16,rating:3,description:`A 12th-century keep with four corner turrets above Thun's old town, housing a history museum and a knights' hall with sweeping views.`,tip:`Walk the covered stairway up from the old town, then the arcaded double-level Obere Hauptgasse below.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Thun Castle`},{id:`oberhofen-castle`,name:`Oberhofen Castle`,localName:`Schloss Oberhofen`,category:`culture`,tags:[`castle`,`lakeside`,`gardens`,`photo-spot`],area:`Oberhofen`,lat:46.72968,lng:7.66857,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:16,rating:4,description:`A fairy-tale castle whose turret stands in the waters of Lake Thun, with furnished period rooms and a lakeside landscape garden.`,tip:`The museum opens mid-May to October and is closed Mondays; the garden is free and open longer.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Oberhofen Castle`},{id:`paragliding-interlaken`,name:`Tandem Paragliding`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`paragliding`,`adrenaline`,`aerial-view`,`tandem`],area:`Höhematte`,lat:46.68624,lng:7.85826,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:230,rating:4,description:`Fly tandem with a pilot from Beatenberg over the town and the two lakes, landing on the Höhematte meadow in the middle of Interlaken.`,tip:`Book the day before and go in the morning; flights are cancelled in strong wind or rain.`,indoor:!1},{id:`unterseen-old-town`,name:`Unterseen Old Town`,localName:`Unterseen`,category:`culture`,tags:[`old-town`,`river`,`walking`,`free`],area:`Unterseen`,lat:46.68692,lng:7.8494,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`Across the Aare from Interlaken, a small medieval town square with a church tower, old wooden houses and quiet riverside paths.`,tip:`Walk over from Interlaken West in ten minutes along the river, ideal for an evening stroll.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Unterseen`},{id:`hoheweg-hohematte`,name:`Höheweg & Höhematte`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`promenade`,`jungfrau-view`,`park`,`free`,`evening-walk`],area:`Interlaken`,lat:46.68601,lng:7.85733,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A protected meadow in the heart of town, kept open so the grand hotels lining the Höheweg promenade keep their framed view of the Jungfrau.`,tip:`Watch paragliders land in the afternoon; at dusk the Jungfrau can glow pink above the hotels.`,indoor:!1},{id:`casino-interlaken`,name:`Casino Interlaken`,localName:`Casino Kursaal`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`casino`,`belle-epoque`,`bar`,`folklore-show`],area:`Interlaken`,lat:46.68825,lng:7.85797,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:2,description:`A Belle Époque Kursaal with a casino, bar and gardens; in summer a Swiss folklore show with yodelling and alphorns runs in the theatre.`,tip:`Bring your passport for the casino; check the summer folklore show dates in advance.`,indoor:!0}],foods:[{name:`Cheese Fondue`,localName:`Käsefondue`,description:`Gruyère and other alpine cheeses melted with white wine in a shared caquelon, eaten with bread and potatoes after a day in the mountains.`},{name:`Raclette`,description:`A wheel of raclette cheese melted and scraped onto boiled potatoes, served with pickled onions and gherkins.`},{name:`Rösti`,description:`Crisp, buttery grated potato cake, in the Bernese Oberland often topped with bacon, melted cheese and a fried egg.`},{name:`Meringue with Double Cream`,localName:`Meringue mit Doppelrahm`,description:`Crunchy meringue shells with thick Gruyère-style double cream; nearby Meiringen claims to be the meringue's birthplace.`},{name:`Berner Platte`,description:`A hearty Bernese platter of smoked and boiled meats and sausages served on sauerkraut, green beans and potatoes.`}]},{id:`zermatt`,name:`Zermatt`,lat:46.02121,lng:7.74925,timezone:`Europe/Zurich`,tagline:`A car-free village beneath the Matterhorn`,description:`A car-free mountain village of larch-wood chalets at the head of the Matter valley, overlooked at every turn by the Matterhorn. Railways and cable cars climb to glaciers, lakes and summits above 3,000 metres, with year-round skiing on the Theodul Glacier and some of the Alps' best hiking in summer.`,idealDays:[2,4],places:[{id:`matterhorn-glacier-paradise`,name:`Matterhorn Glacier Paradise`,localName:`Klein Matterhorn`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`glacier`,`snow`,`cable-car`,`viewpoint`,`iconic`,`high-altitude`],area:`Klein Matterhorn`,lat:45.93833,lng:7.72972,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:160,rating:5,description:`Europe's highest cable-car station at 3,883 metres, with a summit platform looking across 38 four-thousand-metre peaks and onto Mont Blanc and the Italian Alps.`,tip:`Take it slow up there, as the altitude is real; go early in clear weather and check the summit webcam before buying.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Klein Matterhorn`},{id:`glacier-palace`,name:`Glacier Palace`,category:`family`,tags:[`ice-cave`,`glacier`,`sculptures`,`high-altitude`,`kids`],area:`Klein Matterhorn`,lat:45.9381,lng:7.7295,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The world's highest glacier palace, a cave carved 15 metres below the glacier surface at the top station, with ice sculptures and an ice slide.`,tip:`Entry is included with the Matterhorn Glacier Paradise ticket; it is a good option when the summit is in cloud.`,indoor:!0},{id:`gornergrat`,name:`Gornergrat Railway`,localName:`Gornergrat Bahn`,category:`nature`,tags:[`cogwheel-railway`,`viewpoint`,`glacier`,`iconic`,`matterhorn`],area:`Gornergrat`,lat:45.98324,lng:7.78219,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:145,rating:5,description:`A cogwheel railway climbs 33 minutes from Zermatt to 3,089 metres, facing the Matterhorn, Monte Rosa and the vast Gorner Glacier.`,tip:`Sit on the right going up for Matterhorn views; Swiss Travel Pass holders get 50% off.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Gornergrat Railway`},{id:`riffelsee`,name:`Riffelsee`,category:`nature`,tags:[`lake`,`reflection`,`hiking`,`photo-spot`,`matterhorn`],area:`Rotenboden`,lat:45.98336,lng:7.76205,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:110,rating:4,description:`A small mountain lake below the Gornergrat line where, on a still morning, the Matterhorn is mirrored perfectly in the water.`,tip:`Get off at Rotenboden and walk five minutes down; continue on foot to Riffelberg for the next train.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Riffelsee`},{id:`five-lakes-walk`,name:`Five Lakes Walk`,localName:`5-Seenweg`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`hiking`,`lakes`,`reflection`,`matterhorn`,`summer`],area:`Sunnegga / Blauherd`,lat:46.01341,lng:7.80037,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:75,rating:5,description:`A 9 km hike from Blauherd down past Stellisee, Grindjisee, Grünsee, Moosjisee and Leisee, three of which reflect the Matterhorn on calm days.`,tip:`Open roughly late June to October; start at Blauherd early, before the wind ruffles the lakes, and finish at Sunnegga.`,indoor:!1},{id:`sunnegga-leisee`,name:`Sunnegga & Leisee`,localName:`Sunnegga`,category:`family`,tags:[`funicular`,`lake`,`playground`,`kids`,`matterhorn`],area:`Sunnegga`,lat:46.01498,lng:7.77244,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:4,description:`An underground funicular whisks you to a sunny terrace with a classic Matterhorn view; a short walk or free shuttle leads to the Leisee swimming lake and Wolli's adventure park.`,tip:`In summer the Leisee shuttle is free and the lake has a barbecue area and paddling beach for children.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Zermatt–Sunnegga Funicular`},{id:`rothorn`,name:`Rothorn Paradise`,localName:`Unterrothorn`,category:`nature`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`cable-car`,`sunny`,`hiking`],area:`Rothorn`,lat:46.02149,lng:7.79735,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:100,rating:4,description:`The top of the Sunnegga lift system at 3,103 metres, often the sunniest viewpoint around, with the Matterhorn, Weisshorn and Dom in a single sweep.`,tip:`Combine it with the Five Lakes Walk on the same ticket; it gets cloud later than the Gornergrat side.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Unterrothorn`},{id:`schwarzsee`,name:`Schwarzsee`,category:`nature`,tags:[`lake`,`chapel`,`gondola`,`matterhorn`,`hiking`],area:`Schwarzsee`,lat:45.99191,lng:7.70898,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:75,rating:3,description:`A dark little lake with a tiny white chapel at the foot of the Matterhorn's Hörnli ridge, a stop on the gondola towards Trockener Steg.`,tip:`Walk down via Stafelalp and Zmutt for a 3-hour descent through pastures and larch forest.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Schwarzsee (Zermatt)`},{id:`hornli-hut`,name:`Hörnli Hut Hike`,localName:`Hörnlihütte`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`hiking`,`mountain-hut`,`matterhorn`,`strenuous`,`summer`],area:`Hörnli ridge`,lat:45.9822,lng:7.67701,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:75,rating:4,description:`A steep trail from Schwarzsee climbs 700 metres to the mountaineers' hut at 3,260 metres, the base camp for Matterhorn summit attempts.`,tip:`Only for fit hikers with good boots, typically July to September; allow about 2 hours up and start early.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hörnli Hut`},{id:`gorner-gorge`,name:`Gorner Gorge`,localName:`Gornerschlucht`,category:`nature`,tags:[`gorge`,`boardwalk`,`river`,`short-walk`],area:`Gornerschlucht`,lat:46.00879,lng:7.73915,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:3,description:`Wooden walkways and stairs thread through a narrow gorge of green serpentine rock carved by the glacial Gornera, a 20-minute walk from the village.`,tip:`Open roughly June to October; combine it with a walk up to Furi or the Blatten hamlet.`,indoor:!1},{id:`zmutt`,name:`Zmutt Hamlet`,localName:`Zmutt`,category:`culture`,tags:[`hamlet`,`hiking`,`old-chalets`,`free`],area:`Zmutt`,lat:46.00639,lng:7.71694,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A cluster of centuries-old larch barns and a chapel on a meadow shelf, reached by an easy hike from the village with the Matterhorn ahead.`,tip:`Two mountain restaurants here make it a fine lunch walk; return via the Zum See hamlet.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Zmutt`},{id:`hinterdorf`,name:`Hinterdorf Old Quarter`,localName:`Hinterdorf`,category:`culture`,tags:[`old-chalets`,`granaries`,`heritage`,`free`,`walking`],area:`Village`,lat:46.02081,lng:7.7476,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The oldest corner of the village, a lane of blackened larch-wood houses and granaries raised on stone discs to keep out mice.`,tip:`It is tucked behind the main street near the church; go early before the shops open for quiet photos.`,indoor:!1},{id:`matterhorn-museum`,name:`Matterhorn Museum – Zermatlantis`,localName:`Matterhorn Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`mountaineering`,`rainy-day`,`underground`],area:`Kirchplatz`,lat:46.01977,lng:7.74646,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:15,rating:4,description:`An underground museum recreating an old Zermatt village and telling the story of the 1865 first ascent of the Matterhorn and its tragic descent, including the broken rope.`,tip:`Opens in the afternoon and stays open until about 18:00 in summer, handy after a day in the mountains.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Matterhorn Museum`},{id:`st-mauritius-church-cemetery`,name:`St. Mauritius Church & Mountaineers' Cemetery`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`cemetery`,`mountaineering`,`history`,`free`],area:`Kirchplatz`,lat:46.0195,lng:7.74705,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The village church and the small cemetery beside it, where climbers who died on the Matterhorn and surrounding peaks lie under carved ice axes and ropes.`,indoor:!0},{id:`kirchbrucke-matterhorn-view`,name:`Kirchbrücke Matterhorn View`,localName:`Kirchbrücke`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`sunrise`,`sunset`,`free`,`photo-spot`,`iconic`],area:`Village`,lat:46.01891,lng:7.74806,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The bridge over the Matter Vispa by the church is the village's classic Matterhorn viewpoint, best when the peak turns orange at sunrise.`,tip:`Check the sunrise time and arrive 10 minutes early; the light hits the summit before the village.`,indoor:!1},{id:`bahnhofstrasse-zermatt`,name:`Bahnhofstrasse`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`main-street`,`watches`,`outdoor-gear`,`evening-walk`,`free`],area:`Village`,lat:46.02149,lng:7.74683,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The car-free main street from the station to the church, lined with chalet hotels, watch boutiques, outdoor shops, bakeries and bars.`,tip:`Watch for silent electric taxis; shops stay open later in the high season.`,indoor:!1},{id:`papperla-pub`,name:`Papperla Pub`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`pub`,`apres-ski`,`live-music`,`late-night`],area:`Steinmatte`,lat:46.01868,lng:7.74872,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`A buzzing wood-panelled pub that is the village's best-known nightspot, packed after skiing and lively late into the night.`,tip:`Busiest in the winter season; the basement club opens later at weekends.`,indoor:!0},{id:`hennu-stall-apres-ski`,name:`Hennu Stall Après-Ski`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`apres-ski`,`winter`,`music`,`slopes`],area:`Furi`,lat:46.00867,lng:7.73746,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A rowdy après-ski hut on the last run down from Furi, where skiers dance on the terrace in their boots before skiing home in the dusk.`,tip:`Winter only, from about 15:00; the last stretch to the village is an easy piste, but go carefully after drinks.`,indoor:!1},{id:`saas-fee`,name:`Saas-Fee`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`glacier`,`car-free`,`village`,`hiking`],area:`Saas Valley`,lat:46.10967,lng:7.92917,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Another car-free resort in the next valley, ringed by glaciers and thirteen 4,000-metre peaks, with a revolving restaurant and an ice pavilion at Mittelallalin.`,tip:`Reach it by train to Visp or Stalden and PostBus up the valley, about 1.5 to 2 hours each way.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Saas-Fee`}],foods:[{name:`Raclette`,description:`The Valais classic: half a wheel of local raclette cheese melted by the fire and scraped onto potatoes, with pickles and pearl onions.`},{name:`Cheese Fondue`,localName:`Käsefondue`,description:`A bubbling pot of melted cheese with white wine, sometimes laced with tomato or mushrooms in Valais style, eaten with bread and potatoes.`},{name:`Valais Platter`,localName:`Walliser Teller`,description:`Air-dried beef, cured ham, dry sausage, bacon and Valais cheese with rye bread, a classic hut lunch with a glass of local wine.`},{name:`Cholera`,description:`A Valais pie of potatoes, leeks, apples, pears and cheese baked in pastry, named, so the story goes, after the epidemic years.`},{name:`Rösti`,description:`Crispy grated potato cake, in mountain restaurants usually topped with cheese, ham or a fried egg.`}]},{id:`geneva`,name:`Geneva`,localName:`Genève`,lat:46.20167,lng:6.14694,timezone:`Europe/Zurich`,tagline:`Lakeside diplomacy, a giant fountain and Lavaux vineyards`,description:`A cosmopolitan French-speaking city at the tip of Lake Geneva, home to the United Nations, the Red Cross and CERN, with a hilltop old town, lakeside swimming spots and watchmaking museums. Trains and boats run along the shore to the terraced Lavaux vineyards, Montreux and Chillon Castle, while Annecy and the Salève are just over the French border.`,idealDays:[2,4],places:[{id:`jet-d-eau`,name:`Jet d'Eau`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`fountain`,`iconic`,`lake`,`free`,`photo-spot`,`night-view`],area:`Eaux-Vives`,lat:46.20722,lng:6.15611,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Geneva's symbol, a plume of lake water shot 140 metres into the air from a jetty, often crowned by a rainbow on sunny days and lit up after dark.`,tip:`Walk out along the jetty for the spray, but check the wind; it is switched off in strong wind and freezing weather.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Jet d'Eau`},{id:`st-pierre-cathedral`,name:`St. Pierre Cathedral`,localName:`Cathédrale Saint-Pierre`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`cathedral`,`reformation`,`viewpoint`,`archaeology`,`rainy-day`],area:`Old Town`,lat:46.20111,lng:6.14861,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:9,rating:4,description:`The austere cathedral where Calvin preached, crowning the old town; climb the towers for a lake and Alps panorama, and visit the archaeological site beneath it.`,tip:`The nave is free; tower and archaeological site tickets are sold separately or as a combo.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`St. Pierre Cathedral`},{id:`old-town-bourg-de-four`,name:`Old Town & Place du Bourg-de-Four`,localName:`Vieille Ville`,category:`culture`,tags:[`old-town`,`cafes`,`walking`,`free`,`terraces`],area:`Old Town`,lat:46.20024,lng:6.14922,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Steep lanes of grey stone town houses, antique shops and fountains climb to the Bourg-de-Four, the city's oldest square, ringed by café terraces.`,tip:`Look for the long wooden bench on the Promenade de la Treille, said to be the world's longest.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Place du Bourg-de-Four`},{id:`maison-tavel`,name:`Maison Tavel`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`medieval-house`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Old Town`,lat:46.2015,lng:6.14705,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Geneva's oldest private house, now a free museum of everyday city life, with a huge relief model of Geneva as it looked in 1850.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; it is a few steps from the cathedral.`,indoor:!0},{id:`reformation-wall`,name:`Reformation Wall & Parc des Bastions`,localName:`Mur des Réformateurs`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`monument`,`reformation`,`park`,`free`,`giant-chess`],area:`Bastions`,lat:46.20028,lng:6.14556,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A 100-metre wall of statues of Calvin, Farel, Beza and Knox set into the old city ramparts, facing the leafy university park where locals play giant chess.`,tip:`In winter the park hosts an ice rink and a Christmas market.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Reformation Wall`},{id:`jardin-anglais-flower-clock`,name:`Jardin Anglais & Flower Clock`,localName:`L'horloge fleurie`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`garden`,`clock`,`lakefront`,`free`,`photo-spot`],area:`Rive`,lat:46.20419,lng:6.15098,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A lakeside garden whose working clock face of thousands of flowers celebrates Geneva's watchmaking, replanted with the seasons.`,tip:`From here, the lakefront promenade leads to the Jet d'Eau in about 15 minutes.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`L'horloge fleurie`},{id:`palace-of-nations`,name:`Palace of Nations (UN Geneva)`,localName:`Palais des Nations`,category:`culture`,tags:[`united-nations`,`guided-tour`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`],area:`Nations`,lat:46.22667,lng:6.14056,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:28,rating:4,description:`The European headquarters of the United Nations, built for the League of Nations; guided tours visit the Assembly Hall and the Human Rights room with its dripping painted ceiling.`,tip:`Book the tour online and bring your passport for the security check; tours do not run during some major meetings.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Palace of Nations`},{id:`broken-chair`,name:`Broken Chair`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`sculpture`,`landmine`,`free`,`photo-spot`],area:`Nations`,lat:46.2226,lng:6.139,durationHours:.25,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A 12-metre wooden chair with one shattered leg on the Place des Nations, a protest against land mines and cluster bombs facing the UN gates.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Broken Chair`},{id:`red-cross-museum`,name:`International Red Cross and Red Crescent Museum`,localName:`Musée international de la Croix-Rouge`,category:`museum`,tags:[`humanitarian`,`history`,`interactive`,`rainy-day`],area:`Nations`,lat:46.22722,lng:6.13694,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:19,rating:4,description:`A moving, well-designed museum on humanitarian action, with the vast card index of First World War prisoners and personal stories from conflicts and disasters.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; the audio guide is included and pairs well with a UN tour across the road.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`International Red Cross and Red Crescent Museum`},{id:`cern-science-gateway`,name:`CERN Science Gateway`,category:`museum`,tags:[`science`,`physics`,`free`,`interactive`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Meyrin`,lat:46.23397,lng:6.05572,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`CERN's free visitor centre by Renzo Piano, with hands-on exhibitions on particle physics and the Large Hadron Collider, plus the wooden Globe of Science and Innovation.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; tram 18 runs from the city centre. Book free guided tours online as soon as slots open.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`CERN`},{id:`patek-philippe-museum`,name:`Patek Philippe Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`watches`,`craftsmanship`,`automata`,`rainy-day`],area:`Plainpalais`,lat:46.1984,lng:6.13827,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:13,rating:4,description:`Five centuries of watchmaking, from 16th-century pocket watches and enamel miniatures to Patek Philippe's own grand complications.`,tip:`Open Tuesday to Saturday afternoons; free English tours run on Saturdays.`,indoor:!0},{id:`musee-d-art-et-d-histoire`,name:`Museum of Art and History`,localName:`Musée d'Art et d'Histoire`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`archaeology`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Tranchées`,lat:46.1993,lng:6.15157,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Geneva's largest museum with free permanent collections spanning Egyptian antiquities, medieval armour and paintings, including Konrad Witz's altarpiece showing the lake.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; temporary exhibitions charge an entry fee.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée d'Art et d'Histoire (Geneva)`},{id:`musee-ariana`,name:`Musée Ariana`,category:`museum`,tags:[`ceramics`,`glass`,`palace`,`rainy-day`],area:`Nations`,lat:46.2254,lng:6.1388,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The Swiss museum of ceramics and glass in an Italianate palace beside the UN, with a grand domed hall full of porcelain and contemporary glass.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; the permanent collection is free.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée Ariana`},{id:`botanical-garden`,name:`Geneva Botanical Garden`,localName:`Conservatoire et Jardin botaniques`,category:`nature`,tags:[`garden`,`greenhouses`,`free`,`lakeside`,`kids`],area:`Nations`,lat:46.22612,lng:6.14617,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Free gardens and tropical greenhouses running down towards the lake, with a rock garden, a small animal park and a café.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Geneva Botanical Garden`},{id:`parc-la-grange`,name:`Parc La Grange Rose Garden`,localName:`Parc La Grange`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`roses`,`lake-view`,`free`,`picnic`],area:`Eaux-Vives`,lat:46.20627,lng:6.16704,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A sloping lakeside park around an 18th-century villa, with Switzerland's largest public rose garden, in full bloom in June.`,tip:`Continue along the shore to the Genève-Plage and Baby-Plage swimming spots in summer.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Parc La Grange`},{id:`bains-des-paquis`,name:`Bains des Pâquis`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`swimming`,`lake`,`sauna`,`local`,`jet-d-eau-view`],area:`Pâquis`,lat:46.21036,lng:6.15419,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:3,rating:4,description:`A much-loved 1930s lake bath on a jetty, with diving boards, sunbathing on the rocks in summer, saunas and a Turkish bath in winter, and views of the Jet d'Eau.`,tip:`Entry is a couple of francs in summer; in winter the buvette serves fondue on the pier.`,indoor:!1},{id:`lake-geneva-cruise`,name:`Lake Geneva Cruise`,localName:`Lac Léman`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`boat`,`lake`,`belle-epoque`,`scenic`,`sunset`],area:`Mont-Blanc`,lat:46.2079,lng:6.1495,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`Belle Époque paddle steamers and panoramic boats sail from the city quays past lakeside villas and parks, with Mont Blanc in view on clear days.`,tip:`For a cheap ride, the little yellow Mouettes shuttle boats cross the harbour on a regular public transport ticket.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lake Geneva`},{id:`carouge`,name:`Carouge`,category:`culture`,tags:[`old-town`,`artisans`,`cafes`,`mediterranean`,`evening`],area:`Carouge`,lat:46.1836,lng:6.1393,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A town built by the kings of Sardinia, with low Italianate houses, hidden courtyards, artisan workshops and a relaxed bar and restaurant scene.`,tip:`Tram 12 or 18 gets you there in 15 minutes; Wednesday and Saturday mornings bring a market to the main square.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Carouge`},{id:`plainpalais-flea-market`,name:`Plainpalais Flea Market`,localName:`Marché aux puces de Plainpalais`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`flea-market`,`vintage`,`local`,`free`],area:`Plainpalais`,lat:46.1978,lng:6.14174,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A big open-air flea market on the diamond-shaped Plaine de Plainpalais, full of vintage clothes, records, furniture and curios.`,tip:`Held on Wednesdays and Saturdays; arrive early for the best finds and bring cash.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Plainpalais`},{id:`rue-du-rhone`,name:`Rue du Rhône Shopping`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`watches`,`luxury`,`chocolate`,`free`],area:`Rive`,lat:46.20358,lng:6.15023,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Geneva's grand shopping street of watchmakers and jewellers, with chocolatiers and department stores in the lanes between it and the old town.`,tip:`Most shops close on Sundays; the parallel Rue du Marché has more affordable shops.`,indoor:!1},{id:`grand-theatre-de-geneve`,name:`Grand Théâtre de Genève`,category:`culture`,tags:[`opera`,`ballet`,`performance`,`architecture`],area:`Place de Neuve`,lat:46.20178,lng:6.14263,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:80,rating:3,description:`Geneva's 19th-century opera house, modelled on the Paris Opéra, staging opera and ballet from September to June.`,tip:`Last-minute discounted seats are often available for under-26s and on the day.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Grand Théâtre de Genève`},{id:`paquis-bars`,name:`Pâquis Bars & Eateries`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`multicultural`,`late-night`,`local`],area:`Pâquis`,lat:46.2108,lng:6.148,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`The lively, multicultural district behind the lakefront hotels, packed with small bars, cheap world-food eateries and pavement terraces.`,tip:`Start with a drink on the Bains des Pâquis jetty at sunset, then wander inland along Rue de Berne and Rue des Pâquis.`,indoor:!1},{id:`saleve`,name:`Salève Cable Car`,localName:`Téléphérique du Salève`,category:`nature`,tags:[`cable-car`,`viewpoint`,`hiking`,`paragliding`,`france`],area:`Étrembières (France)`,lat:46.1628,lng:6.18917,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:22,rating:4,description:`Just over the French border, a cable car climbs to the Salève ridge, Geneva's balcony, with the whole lake, city and Mont Blanc spread out below.`,tip:`Take bus 8 to Veyrier-Douane and walk across the border; bring your passport and check the last cable car down.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Salève`},{id:`lavaux-vineyards`,name:`Lavaux Vineyard Terraces`,localName:`Lavaux`,category:`food`,tags:[`vineyards`,`wine-tasting`,`unesco`,`hiking`,`day-trip`],area:`Lavaux`,lat:46.49194,lng:6.74611,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:5,description:`UNESCO-listed vineyard terraces stepping down to Lake Geneva between Lausanne and Vevey, with walking trails between wine villages and cellars pouring local Chasselas.`,tip:`Take the train to Cully or Chexbres, walk the terraces to Epesses or St-Saphorin, and taste in a village caveau.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lavaux`},{id:`chillon-castle`,name:`Chillon Castle & Montreux`,localName:`Château de Chillon`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`castle`,`lakeside`,`medieval`,`day-trip`,`iconic`],area:`Veytaux / Montreux`,lat:46.41417,lng:6.9275,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:19,rating:5,description:`A medieval water castle on a rock in the lake, with dungeons immortalised by Byron; a flower-lined promenade leads from it to Montreux and the Freddie Mercury statue.`,tip:`Take the train to Montreux (about 1 hour), walk the 45-minute lakeside path to the castle, and return by paddle steamer in summer.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Chillon Castle`},{id:`annecy`,name:`Annecy`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`canals`,`old-town`,`lake`,`france`],area:`Annecy (France)`,lat:45.8992,lng:6.1288,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A French Alpine town of pastel houses and flower-decked canals on a startlingly clear lake, under an hour from Geneva by bus.`,tip:`Buses leave from Geneva's bus station; bring your passport and some euros, and try the Tuesday, Friday and Sunday markets.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Annecy`},{id:`yvoire`,name:`Yvoire`,category:`culture`,tags:[`medieval-village`,`day-trip`,`boat`,`flowers`,`france`],area:`Yvoire (France)`,lat:46.37028,lng:6.32615,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A walled medieval fishing village on the French shore of the lake, overflowing with flowers, with a labyrinth-like garden of the five senses.`,tip:`In summer arrive by CGN boat from Geneva for the best approach; bring euros.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Yvoire`}],foods:[{name:`Filets de perche`,description:`Lake perch fillets pan-fried in butter, served with lemon, tartare sauce or a lemony butter sauce and French fries.`},{name:`Longeole`,description:`Geneva's protected pork sausage flavoured with fennel seed, slow-poached and served with potatoes or lentils in winter.`},{name:`Malakoff`,description:`A Vaud speciality from the lakeside wine villages: a deep-fried ball of Gruyère cheese on bread, eaten hot with a glass of white wine.`},{name:`Fondue moitié-moitié`,description:`The Romandy classic fondue made half with Gruyère and half with Vacherin Fribourgeois, creamy and nutty.`},{name:`Gratin de cardons`,description:`A creamy, cheesy gratin of Geneva's protected spiny cardoons, the traditional Christmas side dish.`}]}]};export{e as switzerland};